[2026-03-15T01:17:04.051Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CPop99zwH5vEAwoWBXyw2o","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for examining https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- React component tree analysis\n- Expression evaluation and logpoints\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before using tools to identify relevant events, understand their causes, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nA \"Point\" represents a specific execution moment, while an \"Element\" refers to a particular DOM element independent of any specific point in time."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2919a3bc-31f3-44d1-8891-e67557ae62de","uuid":"dbcfde44-6286-4c61-9a02-5cc0e978e3d4","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for examining https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection and searching\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point descriptions with variable values\n- React component tree analysis\n- Expression evaluation and logpoints\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before using tools to identify relevant events, understand their causes, form hypotheses, and support conclusions with gathered data.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nA \"Point\" represents a specific execution moment, while an \"Element\" refers to a particular DOM element independent of any specific point in time.","durationMs":2649,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T01:17:04.515Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7ZCie4y6viC85EnV8zfxj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Getting Started\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings to the cloud\n- **`replayio list`** - View all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login`** / **`replayio logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check installed version info\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps`** - Upload source maps for debugging\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nFor additional details on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2919a3bc-31f3-44d1-8891-e67557ae62de","uuid":"44917b1f-0c53-4d2f-8c3f-9ed540bc8139","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Getting Started\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launch Replay Browser and record a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Upload recordings to the cloud\n- **`replayio list`** - View all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login`** / **`replayio logout`** - Manage account access\n- **`replayio info`** - Check installed version info\n- **`replayio upload-source-maps`** - Upload source maps for debugging\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nFor additional details on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag.","durationMs":4003,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
